{"id": "EUVD-2026-93962", "enisaUuid": "630c62d0-c9c6-3f0f-b799-827d4228b11f", "description": "On affected Arista Wi-Fi access points with captive portal, or application firewall enabled on at least one SSID, a vulnerability in the wireless gateway service could allow an unauthenticated network-adjacent attacker to send a crafted packet that triggers a stack overflow, resulting in a denial-of-service condition or potentially execute arbitrary code on the device. The wireless gateway service is automatically restarted after a crash, allowing repeated exploitation attempts.", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T19:40:29", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-06T20:06:08", "baseScore": 9.4, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:A/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:H/SI:H/SA:H", "references": ["https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/24809-security-advisory-0193"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-102162", "GHSA-qv6j-g65v-6hcc"], "assigner": "Arista", "epss": 0.25, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "02a2cab0-0245-38cf-ab0e-18694995e282", "product": {"name": "Wi-Fi Access Points", "vendor": {"name": "Arista Networks"}}, "product_version": "22.0.0 \u226422.0.1F-32"}, {"id": "0f674a6c-9ccb-3539-8d17-58af2d30a686", "product": {"name": "Wi-Fi Access Points", "vendor": {"name": "Arista Networks"}}, "product_version": "21.3.0 \u226421.3.0M-13"}, {"id": "1a1dde60-257c-32e7-96bf-5f11a8a78491", "product": {"name": "Wi-Fi Access Points", "vendor": {"name": "Arista Networks"}}, "product_version": "1.0.0 <21.3.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "8eb3386a-3e58-3aaf-8c5c-adb30142424a", "vendor": {"name": "Arista Networks"}}], "isExploited": false}